msgid "Both wholesalers are read straight from their own APIs, and the catalogue is built from what they actually sell. Nobody types a destination in: the sync creates the countries the suppliers cover, gives each one its tariff ladder, and records every supplier's price for every tariff."
msgstr "Ikkala ulgurji ta’minotchi ham o‘z API’laridan o‘qiladi va katalog ular haqiqatan sotadigan narsadan quriladi. Yo‘nalishni hech kim qo‘lda kiritmaydi: sinxronizatsiya ta’minotchilar qamrab olgan davlatlarni yaratadi, har biriga tarif pog‘onasini beradi va har bir tarif uchun har bir ta’minotchining narxini yozib qo‘yadi."

msgid "Both suppliers' prices are kept, not just the winner. The cheapest available one becomes the tariff's cost and the route a paid order takes; the dearer one stays on file as the fallback for when the winner is out of stock or its API is down. Customers never see any of this — they see one tariff at one price."
msgstr "Ikkala ta’minotchining narxi ham saqlanadi, faqat g‘olibi emas. Eng arzon mavjudi tarifning tannarxi va to‘langan buyurtma boradigan yo‘l bo‘ladi; qimmatrog‘i g‘olib zaxirada qolmaganda yoki API’si ishlamaganda ishlatiladigan zaxira sifatida qoladi. Mijozlar bularning hech birini ko‘rmaydi — ular bitta tarifni bitta narxda ko‘radi."

msgid "Supplier costs move retail prices through the pricing rules, so a sync can change what the site charges. That is the point, and it is also why a preview writes nothing and why newly discovered destinations arrive switched off — waiting for someone to look at them before they go on sale."
msgstr "Ta’minotchi tannarxi narxlash qoidalari orqali chakana narxni harakatga keltiradi, ya’ni sinxronizatsiya sayt oladigan pulni o‘zgartirishi mumkin. Buning maqsadi shu — va shuning uchun ko‘rib chiqish hech narsa yozmaydi va yangi topilgan yo‘nalishlar o‘chirilgan holda keladi: sotuvga chiqishdan oldin kimdir ularga qarab chiqishi kerak."

